  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    A Nightshelf ceremonial seal-dagger forged during the Great Thaw's first guild charters, bearing the spiraling glyph of ☽'ofund' Guild — the Nightshelf trade faction that rose from volcanic depths to control commerce through Wane☽ Oncea — on a thumb-wide disc of shadow-steel fused to the pommel. The blade was always secondary to the seal-face: an obsidian authentication device whose authority derived from the Mandatum∴ccord, the Nightshelf's binding framework of witnessed testimony.
    
    ### History of Fracture
    
    The obsidian carries a legible genealogy of damage. The earliest clean break dates to the Faction Wars, when Lovumruius~ Domina, a ☽'ofund' merchant whose later activities would warrant a Shadow Parliament recovery order, drove the blade through a Threshold representative to ratify the Mandatum∴ccord. Hairline cracks accumulated during the Clever Ice Age as the dagger passed between Sleek☽ Caemomot and Dawn Naong, each transaction grinding the face finer. The final deliberate fracture came when Night-Assessor Cevmucsiatum-larv~ snapped the blade against stone rather than seal a pact that would have cost the Collective their deepest caverns.
    
    The dagger was displayed alongside the ☽'somunis' Mist~Record at ☽'scar Ramtatus~ during the Mandatum∴ccord's formal proclamation, serving as ceremonial anchor before the Accord's fragmentation scattered its pieces.
    
    ### Current Disposition
    
    | Fragment | Holder | Notes |
    |---|---|---|
    | Central shard (seal-face) | ☽'ofund' Guild vault, third nested lock | Still impressed as header on Guild trade documents |
    | Pommel-piece | Threshold | Transfer circumstances unrecorded |
    | Blade-tip | Unrecorded | No official record exists |
    
    Ownership claims overlap: both ☽'ofund' Guild and The Midnight Claws, the now-dissolved Nightshelf syndicate, are recorded as holders. The Nightshelf has refused to reforge what was shattered. Fire-ash from the dagger's long service stains the grip permanently, and the ☽'ofund' shard continues stamping trade documents — authenticating by habit what it cannot authenticate by right.
